From dd129ab43576b5390037adf1bae0ed71be265d09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:55:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(ui): close the tool library window's gaps to the
 mock-up

The #3663 mock-up and the scope comments on #3897 list five gaps between
the merged U1 to U5 and the design. All are display only:

- The editor stands in two columns: the tabs and their rows on the
  left, the preview on the right.
- The preview gets Dimensions and Holder toggles (view state). Holder
  off shows the model without the holder in 3D, and the side view
  without the holder bands and holder dimensions.
- Each Document row starts with a small drawing of the tool (cached by
  tool name, keyed on the tool value) and has a Gauge length column
  (holder gauge length plus stick-out).
- The categories (from the tool kind) stand on the left of the list.
- The window opens wide enough for the Recipes table and the preview
  side by side, left of the Properties pane, as far as the screen
  permits.

Pinned by tool_library_mockup::* and the updated layout_window_tool_*.

Refs #3897

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
